{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Whoever is for HaShem, to me.</b> Whoever stood in the fear of HaShem and did not sin with the calf — let him come to me immediately. And all the children of Levi gathered to him, for it was an entire tribe from which not a single man was missing. But the rest of the tribes — no whole tribe was found. Therefore it is written of them: ״who said to his father and to his mother, I have not seen him״ — in the matter of the calf; ״and his brothers he did not recognize״ — in the calf; ״and his sons he did not know״ — in the calf; for all of them kept His word, unlike the rest of the tribes. And it appears that since the tribe of Levi was close to Moses, therefore not one of them agreed to deviate from his practice. And in the book of the Rambam, of blessed memory, he says that Abraham transmitted the tradition of Torah to Isaac, and Isaac to Jacob, and Jacob to Levi and his offspring, and they established study halls from which Torah never ceased at all; and therefore they were not enslaved in Egypt, for they engaged in no labor in their days but only in Torah. And it appears that there were three groups in the matter of the calf: one group said ״who shall go before us״ — and they intended only for a leader alone. And another group accepted it as idolatry — and they are the three thousand men who were judged by the sword. And the tribe of Levi — all of them cleaved to HaShem."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:33.055793466Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}